<title>JAPAN: Asahi Bank shares nudge down on Fed $5 mln penalty.</title>
<headline>Asahi Bank shares nudge down on Fed $5 mln penalty.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Asahi Bank Ltd nudged down in early trade on Friday, following news that the Federal Reserve had fined Asahi and its New York branch $5 million for misconduct.</p>
<p>The share price of the bank fell three yen to 810 yen at 0012 GMT, in a volume of 162,000.  </p>
<p>The Fed and the New York State Banking Department also jointly issued a cease and desist order against the bank.</p>
<p>Asahi Bank told Reuters on Friday that it would maintain its U.S. operations despite fines imposed by the Fed.</p>
</text>
